{"name":"Colonnade Grey","hex":"#b2b1ad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"colonnade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A series of columns at regular intervals.","A peristyle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colonnade"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Colonnade","blocks":[{"text":"In classical architecture, a colonnade is a long sequence of columns joined by their entablature, often free-standing, or part of a building. Paired or multiple pairs of columns are normally employed in a colonnade which can be straight or curved. The space enclosed may be covered or open. In St. Peter's Square in Rome, Bernini's great colonnade encloses a vast open elliptical space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Wikimedia_Conference_2015_photo_by_Pine_-_28.jpg/330px-Wikimedia_Conference_2015_photo_by_Pine_-_28.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colonnade"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Luxor_Temple_R07.jpg/330px-Luxor_Temple_R07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th